 are a community in which all are welcomed and respected, and where all can pursue and achieve their highest objectives for themselves, their community, and the world. We value our differences, our environment, and our individual and collective contributions and openly embrace freedom of ideas, inquiry, and expression.\nOur department combines the best features of a small liberal arts college and a major research university. We are a moderately sized department with internationally renowned and accessible faculty dedicated to excellence in research and teaching. Our degree programs have substantial room for electives. This flexibility produces a broad range of customized study plans available to our students.\nA degree in physics or physics and astronomy can be applicable to a wide range of careers including:\nCutting edge research\nEducation\nComputer science\nMedicine\nCommunication\nFinance\nEnvironmental science\nLaw\nBusiness\nEngineering\nSpace and earth sciences\nInterested in applying? Visit our applying page for instructions and a link to our online application.\nContact\nHave questions? Contact Linda Case at grad@pas.rochester.edu.\nReport a Digital Accessibility Barrier\nSite footer\nDepartment of Physics and Astronomy\nVisit\nApply\nCareers\nGive\nLocation\nUniversity of Rochester\n206 Bausch and Lomb Hall\nP.O. Box 270171\nRochester, NY 14627-0171\nPhone\n(585) 275-4351\nResources for\nProspective students\nCurrent students\nParents & families\nFaculty & staff\nAlumni\nHelpful links\nBlackboard\nContact\nDirectory\nHuman resources\nInformation technology\nMyPath\nmyURHR\nParking & shuttles\nUR Mobile (app)\nSchools & divisions\nSchool of Arts & Sciences\nHajim School of Engineering\nEastman School of Music\nSchool of Medicine & Dentistry\nSchool of Nursing & Health Sciences\nSimon Business School\nWarner School of Education\nLaboratory for Laser Energetics\nLibraries & collections\nUniversity Libraries\nMemorial Art Gallery\nEver better\nAccessibility\n